    accessCaveats: ['Meadowood is an unimproved walk-down trail below Upper Falls Dam. Never paddle upstream toward the dam and do not assume a portage exists around it.', 'Lower Falls is listed as a pull-off rather than a developed ramp; confirm the shoreline, shoulder parking, and safe egress before launch.', 'This card ends at the upper shoals/Lower Falls boundary. Do not continue downstream into C-3 or land at private banks without a separately verified access plan.'], watchFor: ['USGS 03200500 discharge outside the 200–5,000 cfs conservative screen, a sharp rise, or a mismatch between Tornado telemetry and the lower reach.', 'Upper Falls Dam boundary upstream, Lower Falls shoals, shallow riffles, strainers, submerged debris, private banks, cold water, traffic/rail crossings, and limited cell service.'], seasonNotes: 'Late spring through fall; September is attractive when Tornado telemetry is stable, recent rainfall is limited, water-quality notices are clear, and both public access points are open.', difficultyNotes: 'Easy Class I moving water for prepared beginners, but the unimproved Meadowood launch and Lower Falls take-out require a deliberate carry and shoreline plan.', confidenceNotes: 'High corridor and endpoint confidence from the Coal River brochure and WVDNR inventory; the 200–5,000 cfs screen is a conservative April–October USGS daily-mean inference rather than an official C-2 runnable range.', shuttle: 'Leave the shuttle at Lower Falls, then return south on Coal River Road/County Route 3 to Meadowood Park. Keep vehicles in public parking, avoid the dam area, and confirm the pull-off is safe for a shuttle vehicle.'
