    safetyNotes: ['The Coal River Water Trail brochure names L-3 as a 12-mile float from the Boone County Water Park north ramp toward the Corridor G / US 119 bridge and also describes a longer approximately 15-mile/4–5-hour drift. The brochure\'s printed bridge coordinate lands off the Little Coal channel near Fuquay Creek, so this card uses the WVDNR-listed The Forks of Coal public access as the auditable take-out while retaining the named 12-mile route label.', 'Danville telemetry is upstream of this reach and is only a proxy. Little Coal can rise quickly after rain and the lower corridor includes shallow riffles, restoration structures, strainers, submerged debris, private banks, and road/bridge crossings.', 'This is a long, low-exit float. Wear a fitted PFD, carry a float plan, food, water, repair kit, first aid, and communications backup. The Forks of Coal endpoint is a public lot, but do not land on adjacent private, railroad, or highway property.'],
